  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Qualify four candidate public static Math Discovery CLR signatures by reflecting real freshly compiled .NET 10 assemblies. Preserve the RS131 CSharp portable protocol and source pins while keeping all 541 native DWF nodes unchanged. Generate no skill, API adapter or public package.",
    "value": "The bounded RS132 preparation stages a source-pinned decision, four-method matrix and BCL-only reflection verifier. A locked restore and Release composition build produce current Math dependencies, then exact parameter/return-type reflection emits four canonical SHA-256 signatures. The evidence explicitly refuses compiled invocation examples, generated skills, BrokerReady, serializable adapters, cross-repository interoperability and any new DWF work package. The M3-W03 proposal stays unadmitted until supported DWF topology authoring is available.",
    "nextAction": "Following a verified RS132, confirm a supported DWF M3-W03 work-package admission before writing compiled invocation examples or deterministic manifest/skill generation. Stage D coordination only after admitted B; any outward recipient transmission requires explicit separate authorization.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "Reflected signatures do not demonstrate compiled method invocation examples or externally routable AURA agent tools.",
      "Math-installed DWF 0.1.59 has no currently admitted new-work-package authoring for proposed M3-W03; issue #139 remains feedback.",
      "The 13 portable Decision fixtures and four reflected Math methods do not certify actual Math/Decision runtime interoperability or BrokerReady.",
      "No public NuGet, ABI/RID compatibility, generated Math skill, external transmission or new M8; the 541 done native nodes remain unchanged."
    ],
    "achievements": []
  },
